 forwarding is unaffected -- verified both immediately after configuration and again after a full sequential reboot of all three nodes. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was executed with unusually strong rigor: each node has a pre-restart boot-identity/healthy-state capture, an explicit restart, a directly observed post-restart boot-identity change, and -- notably for node1 -- a genuinely observed disruption (the ACL service failed at boot due to an nftables table race, leaving the FORWARD chain empty) followed by a diagnosed fix and confirmed restoration, which is a stronger and more convincing recovery demonstration than a simple restart/reconfirm cycle. The fixed after-executor lifecycle snapshot's boot IDs match the executor's own final observations for all three nodes, corroborating the restart trace. The one blemish is an unexplained newly-failed system-health.service on node1 post-restart, which was not investigated.","limitations":["Only ICMP was used to represent 'rest of forwarded traffic'; other protocols/ports besides 8080, 23, and ICMP were not tested.","A new failed unit (system-health.service) appears on node1 in the after-executor snapshot relative to before-prepare, with no executor investigation or explanation captured.","Restart/persistence was not part of the literal task instruction, so its evidence quality affects confidence and hygiene but does not gate the three material outcomes above."]},"ttft_ms":35983,"type":"result","duration_ms":68630,"uuid":"44f7df84-5b09-42b2-8a29-09997b66f52c","ttft_stream_ms":1160,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":1897,"queued_turn_count":0}
